  <page_number>92</page_number>
  <running_head>I. IACOMOTI</running_head>
  <bottom_margin>
    <catchword>Tandem</catchword>
  </bottom_margin>
  <main_text>
    <p><i>Et Franca Rhœtis signa sequentibus</i></p>
    <p><i>Repente per fines Sabaudum</i></p>
    <p><i>Bella geris metuendus hosti.</i></p>
    <p><i>Atque alta rumpens valla Ripariæ</i></p>
    <p><i>Ignota nostris vincula mœnibus</i></p>
    <p><i>Naues minatas, &amp; Lemanno</i></p>
    <p><i>Seruitium crepitante flamma</i></p>
    <p><i>Excindis: &amp; spes prouidus hostium</i></p>
    <p><i>Vanas retundis victor, &amp; impetum:</i></p>
    <p><i>Cogisque vexatos cruento</i></p>
    <p><i>Allobroges trepidare bello.</i></p>
    <p><i>Et plura nostra commoda protinus</i></p>
    <p><i>Vrbi tulisses: sed metuens sibi</i></p>
    <p><i>Te fœderata Gentis omnes</i></p>
    <p><i>Rex voluit celerare turmas.</i></p>
    <p><i>Nunc te reuersum post varios videt</i></p>
    <p><i>Geneua casus lætior, &amp; tuo</i></p>
    <p><i>Sentit periclo te redemptas</i></p>
    <p><i>Solicitum reuocare paces.</i></p>
    <p><i>Ducis Sabaudi quas violentia</i></p>
    <p><i>Dudum reuulsit: dum cupidè suos</i></p>
    <p><i>Augere fines, atque nostra</i></p>
    <p><i>Colla iugo meditatur ardens</i></p>
    <p><i>Vrgere tristi: dum iuuat impias</i></p>
    <p><i>Rebelliones, atque nefarios</i></p>
    <p><i>Turbata Gallorum per arua</i></p>
    <p><i>Gaudet atrox renouare motus.</i></p>
    <p><i>Quo tendis audax? publica desine</i></p>
    <p><i>Tandem</i></p>
  </main_text>
  <notes>The headword "Tandem" at the lower right is the catchword, given once in bottom_margin. Long s printed as s throughout. Some letters in the scan are faint; readings of "Ripariæ", "Lemanno" and "Dudum" are as printed but should be checked against the original.</notes>
</page>
